    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "claim",
      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Connected edge sewing requires an absent arity-two Carrier unit",
      "status": "established_for_stable_even_polygon_carrier_family",
      "demonstrated_strength": [
        "unbounded boundary-pushout theorem",
        "exact all-even framed positive control"
      ],
      "body": "The framed fs/Kato certificates at arities 8, 10, and 12 and the general even-arity induction all pass: primitive four-point coefficient lines external-product coherently, so that positive result is retained. At Carrier level, sewing two marked polygon boundaries along one edge is the pushout of their boundary sets over the edge's two endpoints, hence its arity law is n_L star n_R = n_L+n_R-2. An object unit must solve n star e=n, uniquely forcing e=2. The admitted stable even family begins at arity 4, so the interface-only unit is absent. The four-point factor has residual (n star 4)-n=2 for every n and is therefore not a Carrier unit. Its 'primitive unit' role is the chosen +1 generator of a framed rank-one coefficient line, not an object-level unit law. Boundary excess n-2 is additive under sewing; no initial-semiring multiplication follows.",
      "entity_id": "claim:5a2b6d3a611737304bfd"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "test",
      "kind": "test",
      "title": "Exact connected-sewing boundary-pushout and unit-arity test",
      "status": "passed",
